---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Navbar from "../components/Navbar.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
---

<Base
    title="Company, KYDE"
    description="KYDE builds the behavioral system of record for autonomous work: identity, capabilities, enforcement and evidence in one layer you own. Based in Germany. Built for industries where failure has consequences."
>
    <Navbar />

    <main>

        <!-- ══════════ HERO ══════════ -->
        <section class="relative overflow-hidden">
            <div class="bg-grid absolute inset-0 pointer-events-none"></div>
            <div class="relative max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 pt-36 pb-24 md:pt-48 md:pb-36 md:border-x md:border-line-0">

                <div class="mb-10">
                    <div class="flex items-end justify-between border-b border-line-0 pb-3"><span class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-ink-1">01 · Company</span></div>
                </div>

                <h1 class="hero-h1 max-w-4xl text-4xl font-bold text-ink-0 uppercase tracking-tight md:text-5xl lg:text-6xl">
                    We build the workers, and the layer they run on.
                </h1>
                <p class="mt-8 text-lg text-ink-1 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
                    KYDE turns the processes a company already runs into workers it owns, and runs them inside a zero trust layer that checks every action and keeps the record in the company's own environment.
                </p>

            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- ══════════ BODY ══════════ -->
        <section class="relative border-t border-line-0">
            <div class="relative max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 py-24 md:py-32 md:border-x md:border-line-0">
                <div class="grid md:grid-cols-[200px_1fr] gap-8 items-start">

                    <div>
                        <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-ink-0">About</p>
                        <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-xs text-ink-1">[KYDE]</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="space-y-8 max-w-2xl">
                        <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-1">
                            Companies in banking, insurance, healthcare, manufacturing and the public sector are putting AI into work that has consequences. The processes it lands in were built for people, are documented in outline at best, and answer to regulators.
                        </p>
                        <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-1">
                            Two things are missing. Nobody has written down how the work is actually done, so every automation project starts by guessing. And once something automated starts acting, there is no record of what it did that survives leaving the vendor who made it.
                        </p>
                        <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-1">
                            KYDE does both. We capture one process area with the people who run it, build the part that holds up into a worker, and run it inside KYDE Zero Trust: an identity per worker, policy checked at the moment it acts, sensitive data masked before it reaches a model, and every action hash-chained into a record the company can produce without us.
                        </p>

                        <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-1">
                            Early stage. Engineered in Germany. Working with design partners in finance, insurance, healthcare, the public sector, critical infrastructure and manufacturing.
                        </p>

                        <div class="pt-4">
                            <a
                                href="mailto:hello@kyde.com"
                                class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 border border-line-0 px-6 py-3.5 text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-ink-1 hover:border-line-1 hover:text-ink-0 transition-all"
                            >
                                hello@kyde.com
                            </a>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

    </main>

    <Footer />
</Base>
